  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>To determine the values of x and y, we can use the information provided and the rate expression for the given reaction, which is first order with respect to both A and B:</p><p>Rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mo>]</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mo>]</mo><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>40</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From (i) and (ii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>80</mn></math></p><p>From (i) and (iii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
